---
import TimerPage from '@/layouts/TimerPage.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { faqs } from '@/data/faqs';
import { relatedTimers, relatedPosts } from '@/data/related';
import { defaultConfigs } from '@/engine/presets';
import { meditations } from '@/data/meditations';
---

<TimerPage
  title="Meditation Timer – Interval Bells, Screen Stays On"
  description="Free meditation timer with optional interval bells: 30 minutes with a soft bell every 10 by default, or any length you set. No ticks, no alarm, works offline."
  path="/meditation"
  h1="Meditation timer with interval bells"
  lede="One clock for the whole session, a soft bell every 10 minutes if you want one, and one at the end. Nothing else makes a sound."
  config={defaultConfigs.meditation}
  faq={faqs['/meditation']}
  related={relatedTimers['/meditation']!}
  posts={relatedPosts['/meditation']}
  crumbName="Meditation timer"
>
  <Section title="How it is different" flush>
    <p>
      The other timers on this site are built to be noticed. This one is built to be forgotten.
      The big number is the time left in the whole session; the quiet line under the bar is the
      time to the next bell. Interval bells, the start bell and the end bell are three separate
      switches, so you can have a single bell at the end and silence until then.
    </p>
    <p>
      The default is a 30 minute sit with a bell at 10 and 20 minutes and one to finish. That
      gives three stretches of silence, which is enough structure for a body scan, then breath,
      then open awareness, or simply two reminders to come back.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Presets">
    <p>Each length has its own page with the bells already placed.</p>
    <ul class="links">
      {meditations.map((m) => (
        <li>
          <a href={m.path}>{m.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Screen, sound, silence">
    <p>
      The timer asks the phone or laptop to keep the screen awake while it runs, so the sit does
      not end with a locked phone. Turn the brightness down by hand if you want a dim room. The
      bell is generated in the browser, so there is nothing to download and it works with no
      connection after the first visit.
    </p>
    <p>
      Browsers only play sound from a page that is open, so keep the tab in front rather than
      switching away. Sound Off gives you a fully silent sit where you only glance at the digits.
    </p>
  </Section>
</TimerPage>
